<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>Stocks-Markets-Economic Times</title><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks</link><description><![CDATA[Stock Market News: Latest Stock news and updates on The Economic Times. Find Stock Market Live Updates, BSE, NSE Top Gainers, Losers and more.]]> </description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 05:25:01 +0530</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/2146842.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) 2026 Bennett Coleman and Co. Ltd, http://info.indiatimes.com/terms/tou.html</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>Economic Times</title><url>https://img.etimg.com/thumb/msid-76939477,width-600,height-60/economictimes.jpg</url><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[Sebi sets up sub-group under PMAC to review key IPO norms; NSE's Chauhan to head panel]]> </title><description><![CDATA[Sebi has established a sub-group within its Primary Market Advisory Committee aimed at reassessing regulations related to IPOs and fundraising. The initiative seeks to streamline compliance requirements to foster easier access to capital markets. Key focal points include promoter capital lock-in terms, pricing strategies, and due diligence obligations. The group will evaluate relevant Sebi circulars for potential modifications, with final recommendations to be presented to the PMAC for review.]]> </description><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/sebi-sets-up-sub-group-under-pmac-to-review-key-ipo-norms-nses-chauhan-to-head-panel/articleshow/135890467.cms</link><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://img.etimg.com/photo/msid-135890467,imgsize-80104.cms" length="0"/><guid>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/sebi-sets-up-sub-group-under-pmac-to-review-key-ipo-norms-nses-chauhan-to-head-panel/articleshow/135890467.cms</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 18:37:52 +0530</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Retain capital gains tax on equities, economists tell FM Sitharaman ahead of Budget 2027-28]]> </title><description><![CDATA[Economists recently met with Finance Minister Nirmala Sitharaman to discuss the upcoming Union Budget for 2027-28. They recommended keeping the capital gains tax on equities, opposing industry requests for its abolition. Meeting discussions highlighted the economic improvements and private investment growth, emphasizing the importance of fiscal prudence. Additionally, they suggested boosting the MSME and labor-intensive sectors for employment opportunities.]]> </description><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/retain-capital-gains-tax-on-equities-economists-tell-fm-sitharaman-ahead-of-budget-2027-28/articleshow/135890410.cms</link><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://img.etimg.com/photo/msid-135890410,imgsize-815237.cms" length="0"/><guid>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/retain-capital-gains-tax-on-equities-economists-tell-fm-sitharaman-ahead-of-budget-2027-28/articleshow/135890410.cms</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 18:35:46 +0530</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Sebi forms panel to simplify capital-raising rules]]> </title><description><![CDATA[India's markets regulator has established a 10-member panel to review regulations concerning capital raising by companies. The panel, chaired by Ashish Chauhan of NSE, includes executives from various financial institutions. It will assess eligibility criteria, lock-in periods, and rules for securities allocation and allotment. Furthermore, the group will examine disclosure requirements for initial public offerings and follow-on offers. This initiative aims to simplify regulations and enhance access to capital markets.]]> </description><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/sebi-forms-panel-to-simplify-capital-raising-rules/articleshow/135889803.cms</link><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://img.etimg.com/photo/msid-135889803,imgsize-99926.cms" length="0"/><guid>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/sebi-forms-panel-to-simplify-capital-raising-rules/articleshow/135889803.cms</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 18:14:54 +0530</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[India's investments in US Treasuries jump USD 38.4 bn in Jun-Aug amid FCNR flows]]> </title><description><![CDATA[India's investment in US Treasury securities increased by USD 38.4 billion due to FCNR(B) deposits during three months. The Reserve Bank of India introduced a special facility to encourage these foreign currency deposits. This facility led to significant inflows, improving India's foreign exchange reserves substantially. Experts suggest that investment in US Treasuries may slow down due to the closure of the FCNR(B) window. India's reserves grew to USD 740.]]> </description><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/indias-investments-in-us-treasuries-jump-usd-38-4-bn-in-jun-aug-amid-fcnr-flows/articleshow/135888824.cms</link><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://img.etimg.com/photo/msid-135888824,imgsize-179256.cms" length="0"/><guid>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/indias-investments-in-us-treasuries-jump-usd-38-4-bn-in-jun-aug-amid-fcnr-flows/articleshow/135888824.cms</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 17:47:29 +0530</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[PNB among 4 stocks hitting 52-week highs; stock rallies up to 24% in a month]]> </title><description><![CDATA[Four BSE 100 stocks, including PNB, Eternal, Federal Bank and Kotak Mahindra Bank, touched fresh 52-week highs. Here's how much these stocks have gained over the past month.]]> </description><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/pnb-among-4-stocks-hitting-52-week-highs-stock-rallies-up-to-24-in-a-month/slideshow/135888569.cms</link><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://img.etimg.com/photo/msid-135888524,imgsize-9922.cms" length="0"/><guid>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/pnb-among-4-stocks-hitting-52-week-highs-stock-rallies-up-to-24-in-a-month/slideshow/135888569.cms</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 17:33:47 +0530</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Sebi may propose raising FPI beneficial ownership threshold to 25%; plans consultation paper]]> </title><description><![CDATA[The Securities and Exchange Board of India (Sebi) is contemplating raising the beneficial ownership stake for foreign portfolio investors from 10 percent to 25 percent. This proposed change aims to simplify compliance and bring India in line with global standards. A consultation paper will be released shortly to collect input from stakeholders on easing regulations.]]> </description><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/sebi-may-propose-raising-fpi-beneficial-ownership-threshold-to-25-plans-consultation-paper/articleshow/135883637.cms</link><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://img.etimg.com/photo/msid-135883637,imgsize-94498.cms" length="0"/><guid>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/sebi-may-propose-raising-fpi-beneficial-ownership-threshold-to-25-plans-consultation-paper/articleshow/135883637.cms</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:51:12 +0530</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Swiggy among 10 midcap stocks that dropped up to 50% in CY26]]> </title><description><![CDATA[The Nifty Midcap 150 has gained around 2% in CY26, but several constituents have suffered steep corrections. Swiggy, PI Industries and Rail Vikas Nigam lead the 10 biggest laggards, with losses ranging from 32% to 52%.]]> </description><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/swiggy-among-10-midcap-stocks-that-dropped-up-to-50-in-cy26/slideshow/135883464.cms</link><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://img.etimg.com/photo